{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "08", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "03", "M": "14", "S": "54"}}, "news": [{"title": "Eye on high-rise work resumption, builders in Kolkata start calling back workers to sites", "para": "In Kolkata, construction developers are bringing laborers back to the sites as many halted projects gain the necessary approvals to restart. Contractors are reaching out to the workers who had previously returned home, signaling a resurgence in construction activity expected in just weeks. The industry is positive about the government's newly implemented safety standards, seeing them as a boost to the sector.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/eye-on-high-rise-work-resumption-builders-in-kolkata-start-calling-back-workers-to-sites/133045792?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-228203/133045792.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Decades-old dispute buries \u20b92,000-crore land under mountains of rubble in Hyderabad\u2019s IT hub", "para": "In Hyderabad, a valuable land parcel worth over Rs 2,000 crore has tragically turned into a neglected dumpsite filled with construction waste. Entangled in a longstanding legal battle between a real estate firm and the state government, this land's value skyrocketed from Rs 50 lakh per acre. Now, it hosts massive heaps of debris, prompting the Cyberabad Municipal Corporation to seek effective, scientific solutions for waste clearance.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/decades-old-dispute-buries-2000-crore-land-under-mountains-of-rubble-in-hyderabads-it-hub/133045775?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-365440/133045775.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Delhi government reiterates no existing houses in O-Zone will face demolition action", "para": "The Delhi government confirmed that there are no plans to demolish any existing O-Zone houses. They pointed to current demolitions, requesting legal safeguards for colonies. Delhi Development Minister Kapil Mishra labeled the O-Zone situation as serious, assuring that more than thirty lakh homes are secure.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/delhi-government-reiterates-no-existing-houses-in-o-zone-will-face-demolition-action/133045735?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-36434/133045735.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}